# Schur-Weyl duality context from Maschke's theorem and DCT
%%%
tag := "Chapter5/Discussion_before_Theorem5.18.4"
number := false
%%%

Now, the algebra $`A` is semisimple by Maschke's theorem, so the double centralizer theorem applies, and we get the following result, which goes under the name "Schur-Weyl duality" (as it was discovered by Schur and popularized by Weyl in his books _The theory of groups and quantum mechanics_ and _Classical groups_; see Section 5.20).
